CLASS:: Pulsar
SUMMARY:: Pulsar synthesis with polynomial pulsaret shapes and phase coupling
CATEGORIES:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
RELATED:: Classes/Blip, Classes/Formant, Classes/SyncSaw, Classes/VOsc

DESCRIPTION::
Pulsar implements pulsar synthesis with micro-level synchronization capabilities. Each pulsaret consists of a polynomial envelope code::t^a * (1-t)^b:: modulating a sine carrier.

STRONG::Key Features:::
LIST::
## Polynomial pulsaret envelope with shape control
## Formant control via carrier frequency ratio
## Three synchronization modes: Kuramoto coupling, hard sync, soft sync
## Multiple sync phase inputs for true Kuramoto coupling
## Phase output for coupling multiple oscillators
## Polyphonic pulsarets (width > 1 creates overlaps)
## All parameters modulatable at audio rate
::

SUBSECTION:: Outputs

Pulsar is a MultiOutUGen with two outputs:
LIST::
## code::out[0]:: - Audio signal
## code::out[1]:: - Current phase [0-1] for coupling to other oscillators
::

SUBSECTION:: Pulsaret Shape

The envelope is code::t^a * (1-t)^b:: where t goes from 0 to 1 over the pulsaret duration.
LIST::
## Peak position = a/(a+b)
## Lower values = narrower peak = brighter spectrum
## shapeA controls attack, shapeB controls decay
::

SUBSECTION:: Synchronization Modes

TABLE::
## strong::Mode:: || strong::Value:: || strong::Description::
## Kuramoto || 0 || Computes (K/N) * Σ sin(θ_j - θ_self) for all input phases
## Hard Sync || 1 || Reset phase on first input's wrap (classic sync oscillator)
## Soft Sync || 2 || Reset only if phase > threshold (uses first input only)
::

SUBSECTION:: Kuramoto Coupling

When syncMode is 0, the phase evolves according to the Kuramoto model:

code::
dθ/dt = ω + (K/N) * Σ_j sin(θ_j - θ)
::

The UGen computes the sum of pairwise coupling terms internally when given multiple sync inputs. 

SUBSECTION:: Kuramoto Chaos Regimes

The Kuramoto mode has nonlinear terms that activate at higher coupling strengths:
LIST::
## |K| < 0.5: Simple sinusoidal coupling, stable sync/anti-sync
## |K| > 0.5: Second harmonic term, more complex attraction basins
## |K| > 1.0: Cubic term and third harmonic, chaos possible
## |K| > 1.5: Self-modulation term, rich chaotic dynamics
::


CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: freq
Pulsar train frequency in Hz. Default: 100.

ARGUMENT:: formantRatio
Ratio of formant frequency to fundamental. Default: 1.

ARGUMENT:: width
Duty cycle [0-2]. Values > 1 create overlapping pulsarets. Default: 0.5.

ARGUMENT:: shapeA
Attack shape exponent [0.1-10]. Default: 2.

ARGUMENT:: shapeB
Decay shape exponent [0.1-10]. Default: 2.

ARGUMENT:: mask
Gate signal. When < 0.5 at pulsaret trigger, that pulsaret is silenced. Default: 1.

ARGUMENT:: syncPhases
Phase input(s) from other oscillators [0-1]. Can be a single value or an array of phases. For Kuramoto mode, all phases contribute to the coupling sum. For hard/soft sync, only the first input is used for edge detection. Default: #[0].

ARGUMENT:: syncStrength
Coupling strength. Values > 1 enable chaotic dynamics. Default: 0.

ARGUMENT:: syncMode
Sync mode: 0=Kuramoto, 1=hard, 2=soft. Default: 0.

ARGUMENT:: syncThreshold
For soft sync, phase threshold [0-1]. Default: 0.5.

ARGUMENT:: phase
Initial phase [0-1]. Only read at instantiation. Default: 0.

ARGUMENT:: maxPulsarets
Maximum simultaneous pulsarets [1-16]. Default: 4.


EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Basic Usage

code::
// Simple pulsar - index [0] for audio
{ Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.5)[0] * 0.3 }.play;

// Modulated formant ratio
{ Pulsar.ar(80, SinOsc.kr(0.2).range(2, 12), 0.4)[0] * 0.3 }.play;

// Percussive shape (fast attack, slow decay)
{ Pulsar.ar(60, 6, 0.6, shapeA: 1, shapeB: 5)[0] * 0.3 }.play;

// Overlapping pulsarets (width > 1)
{ Pulsar.ar(40, 8, 1.5, shapeA: 3, shapeB: 3)[0] * 0.3 }.play;
::


SUBSECTION:: Masking (Rhythmic Gating)

code::
// Pulse masking creates rhythmic patterns
(
{
    var mask = LFPulse.ar(4, 0, 0.6);
    Pulsar.ar(200, 5, 0.4, mask: mask)[0] * 0.3
}.play;
)

// Probabilistic masking
(
{
    var trig = Impulse.ar(100);
    var mask = TRand.ar(0, 1, trig) > 0.3;
    Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.5, mask: mask)[0] * 0.3
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Two Coupled Oscillators

code::
// Bidirectional Kuramoto coupling using LocalIn/LocalOut
// Each oscillator receives the other's phase as syncPhases
(
{
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(2);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 0.5);
    
    var p1 = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: 100,
        formantRatio: 4,
        width: 0.4,
        syncPhases: phases[1],  // single phase input
        syncStrength: coupling
    );
    
    var p2 = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: 103,
        formantRatio: 4,
        width: 0.4,
        syncPhases: phases[0],
        syncStrength: coupling,
        phase: 0.5
    );
    
    LocalOut.ar([p1[1], p2[1]]);
    [p1[0], p2[0]] * 0.2
}.play;
)

// Negative coupling - phases repel toward anti-phase
(
{
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(2);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, -0.5);
    
    var p1 = Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.4, syncPhases: phases[1], syncStrength: coupling);
    var p2 = Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.4, syncPhases: phases[0], syncStrength: coupling, phase: 0.1);
    
    LocalOut.ar([p1[1], p2[1]]);
    [p1[0], p2[0]] * 0.2
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: N-Oscillator Kuramoto Network (Multiple Sync Inputs)

code::
// 6 coupled oscillators - each receives ALL OTHER phases as an array
// The UGen internally computes Σ sin(θ_j - θ_self)
(
{
    var n = 6;
    var freqs = Array.fill(n, { exprand(95, 105) });
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(n);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 0.4);
    
    var pulsars = n.collect { |i|
        // Collect all OTHER phases (exclude self)
        var otherPhases = (0..n-1).reject(_ == i).collect { |j| phases[j] };
        
        Pulsar.ar(
            freq: freqs[i],
            formantRatio: 5,
            width: 0.4,
            syncPhases: otherPhases,  // array of phases!
            syncStrength: coupling,
            phase: i / n
        )
    };
    
    LocalOut.ar(pulsars.collect(_[1]));
    Splay.ar(pulsars.collect(_[0])) * 0.15
}.play;
)

// 8 oscillators with spread frequencies
(
{
    var n = 8;
    var freqs = Array.fill(n, { exprand(80, 120) });
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(n);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 0.5);
    
    var pulsars = n.collect { |i|
        var otherPhases = (0..n-1).reject(_ == i).collect { |j| phases[j] };
        
        Pulsar.ar(
            freq: freqs[i],
            formantRatio: LFDNoise1.kr(0.1).range(3, 8),
            width: 0.4,
            syncPhases: otherPhases,
            syncStrength: coupling,
            phase: i / n
        )
    };
    
    LocalOut.ar(pulsars.collect(_[1]));
    Splay.ar(pulsars.collect(_[0])) * 0.12
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Nearest-Neighbor Coupling (Ring Topology)

code::
// Each oscillator couples only to its neighbors
(
{
    var n = 8;
    var freqs = Array.fill(n, { exprand(90, 110) });
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(n);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 0.6);
    
    var pulsars = n.collect { |i|
        // Only couple to immediate neighbors (ring)
        var neighborPhases = [phases.wrapAt(i - 1), phases.wrapAt(i + 1)];
        
        Pulsar.ar(
            freq: freqs[i],
            formantRatio: 4,
            width: 0.45,
            syncPhases: neighborPhases,
            syncStrength: coupling,
            phase: i / n
        )
    };
    
    LocalOut.ar(pulsars.collect(_[1]));
    Splay.ar(pulsars.collect(_[0])) * 0.12
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Hard Sync

code::
// Classic hard sync sweep
(
{
    var master = Pulsar.ar(100, 1, 0.5);
    var slaveFreq = MouseX.kr(100, 800, 1);
    
    var slave = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: slaveFreq,
        formantRatio: 1,
        width: 0.5,
        syncPhases: master[1],
        syncMode: 1  // hard sync
    );
    
    slave[0] * 0.3
}.play;
)

// Modulated hard sync
(
{
    var master = Pulsar.ar(80, 2, 0.4, shapeA: 1, shapeB: 3);
    var slaveFreq = LFNoise1.kr(0.3).exprange(150, 600);
    
    var slave = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: slaveFreq,
        formantRatio: 3,
        width: 0.5,
        shapeA: 2,
        shapeB: 4,
        syncPhases: master[1],
        syncMode: 1
    );
    
    slave[0] * 0.3
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Soft Sync

code::
// Soft sync - threshold controls how often sync occurs
(
{
    var master = Pulsar.ar(100, 1, 0.5);
    var threshold = MouseY.kr(0.1, 0.9);
    
    var slave = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: 310,
        formantRatio: 3,
        width: 0.4,
        syncPhases: master[1],
        syncMode: 2,
        syncThreshold: threshold
    );
    
    slave[0] * 0.3
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Chaotic Dynamics (syncStrength > 1)

code::
// Two oscillators - overcoupling creates chaos
(
{
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(2);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 3);  // past 1.0 = chaos
    
    var p1 = Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.4, syncPhases: phases[1], syncStrength: coupling);
    var p2 = Pulsar.ar(100, 4, 0.4, syncPhases: phases[0], syncStrength: coupling, phase: 0.5);
    
    LocalOut.ar([p1[1], p2[1]]);
    [p1[0], p2[0]] * 0.2
}.play;
)

// N oscillators with overcoupling - all-to-all creates complex dynamics
(
{
    var n = 6;
    var freqs = 100 ! n;  // same frequency - chaos from coupling alone
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(n);
    var coupling = MouseX.kr(0, 2.5);
    
    var pulsars = n.collect { |i|
        var otherPhases = (0..n-1).reject(_ == i).collect { |j| phases[j] };
        
        Pulsar.ar(
            freq: freqs[i],
            formantRatio: 5,
            width: 0.4,
            syncPhases: otherPhases,
            syncStrength: coupling,
            phase: i / n
        )
    };
    
    LocalOut.ar(pulsars.collect(_[1]));
    Splay.ar(pulsars.collect(_[0])) * 0.12
}.play;
)

// Chaotic network with delays
(
{
    var n = 6;
    var freqs = Array.exprand(n, 50, 200);
    var phases = LocalIn.ar(n);
    
    var delayedPhases = phases.collect { |p|
        DelayC.ar(p, 0.1, LFDNoise1.ar(0.5).range(0.005, 0.03))
    };
    
    var pulsars = n.collect { |i|
        // Couple to multiple delayed neighbors
        var syncInputs = [
            delayedPhases.wrapAt(i + 1),
            delayedPhases.wrapAt(i + 2),
            delayedPhases.wrapAt(i - 1)
        ];
        
        Pulsar.ar(
            freq: freqs[i] * LFDNoise1.ar(0.2).range(0.97, 1.03),
            formantRatio: LFDNoise1.ar(0.15).range(2, 8),
            width: LFDNoise1.ar(0.1).range(0.4, 1.6),
            shapeA: LFDNoise1.ar(0.12).exprange(0.3, 5),
            shapeB: LFDNoise1.ar(0.1).exprange(0.3, 4),
            syncPhases: syncInputs,
            syncStrength: LFDNoise1.ar(0.2).range(1.3, 2.5),
            phase: i / n
        )
    };
    
    LocalOut.ar(pulsars.collect(_[1]));
    Splay.ar(pulsars.collect(_[0])) * 0.15
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Phase as Modulation Source

code::
// Phase modulates formant of another Pulsar
(
{
    var p1 = Pulsar.ar(60, 4, 0.5);
    var p2 = Pulsar.ar(
        freq: 120,
        formantRatio: p1[1].linlin(0, 1, 2, 12),
        width: 0.4
    );
    [p1[0], p2[0]] * 0.2
}.play;
)

// Phase controls stereo position
(
{
    var sig = Pulsar.ar(80, 6, 0.5);
    var pan = sig[1] * 2 - 1;
    Pan2.ar(sig[0], pan) * 0.3
}.play;
)
::


SUBSECTION:: Multichannel Expansion

code::
// Array of frequencies
(
{
    var freqs = [100, 150, 200, 250];
    var sig = Pulsar.ar(freqs, 4, 0.4);
    Splay.ar(sig.collect(_[0])) * 0.15
}.play;
)

// Detuned unison
(
{
    var detune = [0.99, 0.997, 1, 1.003, 1.01];
    var sig = Pulsar.ar(100 * detune, 5, 0.45);
    Splay.ar(sig.collect(_[0])) * 0.12
}.play;
)
::

